{"task_id": "Mbpp/90", "solution": "from typing import List, Iterator\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass InputList:\n    items: List[str]\n    def __iter__(self) -> Iterator[str]:\n        return iter(self.items)\n\n@dataclass\nclass StringItem:\n    value: str\n    def length(self) -> int:\n        return len(self.value)\n\n@dataclass\nclass Result:\n    longest_length: int\n\ndef len_log(words: List[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Compute and return the length (number of characters) of the longest string in words.\n\n    Notes: Empty list returns 0. For non-string elements, len() will be called; Python semantics apply.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not words:\n        return 0\n    il = InputList(words)\n    max_len = 0\n    for s in il:\n        si = StringItem(s)\n        l = si.length()\n        if l > max_len:\n            max_len = l\n    return Result(max_len).longest_length"}
