{"task_id": "Mbpp/172", "solution": "PATTERN = \"std\"\n\ndef count_occurance(input_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of occurrences of the string 'std' in a given string.\n    Raises TypeError if the input is not a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"input_string must be a string\")\n\n    count = 0\n    n = len(input_string)\n    m = len(PATTERN)\n\n    if n < m:\n        return 0\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if input_string[i:i+m] == PATTERN:\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/222", "solution": "def check_type(input_tuple: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Accepts a single tuple argument and returns True if all elements have identical runtime types, otherwise False.\n    Behavior: Deterministic, no side effects, single-pass (O(n)).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_tuple:\n        return True  # Empty tuple considered homogeneous (all elements have the \"same\" type vacuously).\n\n    first_type = type(input_tuple[0])\n    for element in input_tuple[1:]:\n        if type(element) != first_type:\n            return False\n    return True"}
