{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "from dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Iterator, Optional\n\n@dataclass\nclass Parameter:\n    l: int\n    r: int\n\n    def as_range(self) -> 'Range':\n        return Range(start=self.l, end=self.r)\n\n@dataclass\nclass Range:\n    start: int\n    end: int\n\n    def iter_values(self) -> Iterator[int]:\n        \"\"\"Iterate over all integer values in the inclusive range [start, end].\"\"\"\n        current = self.start\n        while current <= self.end:\n            yield current\n            current += 1\n\n@dataclass\nclass Number:\n    value: int\n\n    def is_odd(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the number is odd.\"\"\"\n        return self.value % 2 != 0\n\n    def is_natural(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the number is a natural number (positive integer > 0).\"\"\"\n        return self.value > 0\n\n@dataclass\nclass Result:\n    total: int\n\ndef sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Compute sum of all odd natural numbers in inclusive range [l, r].\n    Natural numbers are defined as positive integers (>0) per SRS.\n    \"\"\"\n    params = Parameter(l, r)\n    current_range = params.as_range()\n    \n    total_sum = 0\n    for val in current_range.iter_values():\n        num = Number(val)\n        if num.is_natural() and num.is_odd():\n            total_sum += num.value\n            \n    result = Result(total_sum)\n    return result.total"}
